  "design": [
    "Save only the static scenery fragment before close combat reuses the packet arena. Never retain actors or UI.",
    "Borrow the unchanged exact-key storage across the close view; every key writer increments its generation. Reject changed generations, prefix counts, camera bytes and scenery bytes before staging any saved command.",
    "Keep original encoded DMA base separate from CPU storage. Normal fragment replay relocates internal links and joins the live ordering table. GPU reads retire before writes.",
    "A 52 KiB command backup is bounded by the existing world-command capacity. Missing/invalid snapshots use ordinary current-renderer drawing. Original audio, stack and 512 KiB gameplay heap reserves remain."
  ],
